    "original_title": "Madaxweyne Xasan Sheekh oo kormeeray Taliska Qaybta 1-aad ee Kumaandooska Gorgor",
    "slug": "somali-president-visits-gorgor-commando-brigade-1-headquarters",
    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud made a working visit to the 1st Brigade of the Gorgor Commandos in Mogadishu, inspecting facilities and receiving briefings on troop readiness.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, September 10, 2026 — President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud, who also serves as Commander-in-Chief of the Somali National Armed Forces, conducted a working visit to the headquarters of the 1st Brigade of the Gorgor Commandos in Mogadishu on Thursday. During the visit, the President toured the brigade's offices, troop quarters, field hospital, and logistics facilities, and received briefings from brigade commanders and other military officials.\n\nThe visit allowed the President to directly assess the general condition of the troops, the services they receive, and their level of operational readiness. The Gorgor Commandos are an elite unit within the Somali National Army, trained for counter-insurgency and special operations, and have been central to recent military campaigns against Al-Shabaab. The 1st Brigade is among the most active units in these operations.\n\nHassan Sheikh Mohamud has prioritized strengthening the armed forces since returning to office in 2022. His administration has overseen increased training and equipping of troops, with support from international partners such as the United States, Turkey, and the European Union. The President's visit comes amid ongoing preparations to take over security responsibilities as the African Union Transition Mission in Somalia (ATMIS) continues its phased withdrawal.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the readiness of elite units like the Gorgor Commandos is of particular importance. Many diaspora members have family in areas affected by conflict and rely on the army's ability to maintain security. Additionally, some diaspora Somalis have returned to serve in the security forces or contribute financially to stabilization efforts. A well-functioning army is also seen as essential for attracting investment and enabling reconstruction.\n\nThis visit underscores the federal government's focus on military capacity-building as a cornerstone of its security strategy. It follows similar inspections by the President of other military installations in recent months. The Gorgor Commandos are expected to play a leading role in upcoming operations to secure liberated areas and protect civilian populations.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/10/madaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-oo-kormeeray-taliska-qaybta-1-aad-ee-kumaandooska-gorgor/",
